      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Barbed_wire",
      "label": "Barbed wire",
      "description": "Barbed wire is a type of fencing used to enclose and control access to areas, often associated with prisons, concentration camps, and military installations. In the image, barbed wire is visible in the foreground, indicating the prisoners are confined within a secure, oppressive environment. Understanding the symbolism of barbed wire is necessary to interpret the context of the prisoners' situation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_447ab577"
      },
